	)
	(text "Upper I2C isolation. Discharge protection is out of scope. No charge FET, USB, or CAN.\nU_ISO is the ISO1640 8-pin D pin map from the ISO1640 datasheet Table 5-1. It has no enable pin.\nSide 1 (SDA1/SCL1) faces the host and is limited to 80 pF. Side 2 faces the upper BQ bus and allows 400 pF.\nVCC1 is HOST_3V3, 3 V to 5.5 V. VCC2 is upper REG1, 2.25 V to 5.5 V. Each supply gets 100 nF to its own ground (datasheet 9.2.1).\nGND1 is CELL0. GND2 is CELL16. Those grounds are not connected.\nTMUX154E U204 uses pins 4/2 for SDA host/ISO-side and pins 6/8 for SCL host/ISO-side; pins 3/7 are unused. Pin 1 SEL is low, pin 9 EN is GPIO9, pin 10 VCC is HOST_3V3, pin 5 GND is CELL0.\nU204 EN low connects A/B to A0/B0 (SEL low); EN high opens. GPIO9 high therefore opens at reset, GPIO9 low connects after lower address verification. U204 I/O is high impedance when VCC=0.\nU204 needs VCC 3.0-4.3 V. Powered I/O must stay within 0..VCC; powered-off I/O is rated to 5.25 V. Rail envelope must be checked against HOST_3V3 and lower REG1.\nR201/R202 and lower R20/R21 are pull-ups on opposite sides. Values remain OPEN pending rail-difference current, combined sink current, 80 pF ISO1640 side-1 loading, rise-time and 100 kHz analysis.\nHost/lower-REG1 sequencing and lower-BQ back-power behavior remain OPEN. Baseline C enables ESP32 internal I2C pullups on the same lower bus.\nFirmware must verify lower BQ at 0x10 before GPIO9 low enables upper 0x08.\nUpper SDA/SCL pull-ups already sit on the upper sheet, on REG1_BQ2.\nOPEN parts:\nU_ISO: Bidirectional I2C isolator using the ISO1640 8-D pin map (VCC1, SDA1, SCL1, GND1, GND2, SCL2, SDA2, VCC2). No enable pin. Orderable suffix is OPEN; the 16-DW package has different pin numbers and is not this symbol.\nU204: TI TMUX154EDGSR, 2-channel SPDT switch in VSSOP-10. Pin 4 A and pin 6 B are the host-side SDA/SCL commons; pins 2 A0 and 8 B0 face ISO1640 SDA1/SCL1. Pins 3 A1 and 7 B1 are unused; pin 1 SEL is held low to select A0/B0; pin 9 EN is active low and goes directly to GPIO9; pin 10 VCC is HOST_3V3; pin 5 GND is CELL0. TI specifies 3.0-4.3 V supply, I/O to 5.25 V, and high-impedance I/O when unpowered.\nR201: Switch/ISO1640 side-1 SDA pull-up to HOST_3V3. Resistance remains OPEN pending rail-difference, aggregate sink-current, capacitance and rise-time calculation at 100 kHz.\nR202: Switch/ISO1640 side-1 SCL pull-up to HOST_3V3. Resistance remains OPEN pending rail-difference, aggregate sink-current, capacitance and rise-time calculation at 100 kHz.\nC203: 100 nF local bypass from HOST_3V3 to CELL0.\nALERT_BQ2: Upper ALERT stays on the upper side and ends at a no-connect on this sheet. Do not tie it to CELL0. Firmware does not consume upper ALERT. A unidirectional isolator MPN across the barrier is OPEN; do not invent that part.\nR203: GPIO9 reset pull-up to HOST_3V3. Value is OPEN. GPIO9 must be high at reset because GPIO9 low selects ESP32-C3 download mode; that level disables U204."
		(at 20.32 229.87 0)
